# example objects file with men, women and children of 5 heights: 10 cm smaller, 5 cm smaller, the normal height,
# 5 cm bigger and 10 cm bigger, in 3 rows in front of camera 1 (cameraObjectPosition1=0/1000/0 of
# configs/cameraobjects_ids.ini), every row from the smallest (left) to the biggest (right), all look toward the
# cameras. Open it with:
#     cp examples/objects_people_sizes.dat <cameraImageOutputDirectory>/camera_objects/
#     ./prj-camera-image-creator --objectsFile=objects_people_sizes.dat
#
# A person of another height has all 3 sizes of the normal height scaled the same, so the proportions stay:
# size = normal size * height / normal height, and y = height/2 puts the person on the floor.
# Man: normal 1.80 m = 560/1800/310, Woman: normal 1.65 m = 490/1650/300, Child: normal 1.20 m = 360/1200/215.


# children: 1.10 m, 1.15 m, 1.20 m, 1.25 m, 1.30 m
# 10 cm smaller, 1.10 m
Child=-1800.0/550.0/3500.0/330.0/1100.0/197.1/180.0/0.0/0.0/shirt_green.png
# 5 cm smaller, 1.15 m
Child=-900.0/575.0/3500.0/345.0/1150.0/206.0/180.0/0.0/0.0/shirt_red.png
# normal height, 1.20 m
Child=0.0/600.0/3500.0/360.0/1200.0/215.0/180.0/0.0/0.0/shirt_gray.png
# 5 cm bigger, 1.25 m
Child=900.0/625.0/3500.0/375.0/1250.0/224.0/180.0/0.0/0.0/shirt_white.png
# 10 cm bigger, 1.30 m
Child=1800.0/650.0/3500.0/390.0/1300.0/232.9/180.0/0.0/0.0/shirt_blue.png

